WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.410 --> 00:00:04.920
In Massachusetts, we
know a thing or two about

00:00:04.920 --> 00:00:05.970
revolutionary ideas.

00:00:05.970 --> 00:00:07.570
[GUNFIRE]

00:00:07.570 --> 00:00:10.302
And at MIT, we know a thing
or two about innovation

00:00:10.302 --> 00:00:11.176
and entrepreneurship.

00:00:16.520 --> 00:00:18.850
Together, the
universities, communities,

00:00:18.850 --> 00:00:22.110
and industries of Greater Boston
have transformed this region

00:00:22.110 --> 00:00:23.820
into one of the
hottest innovation

00:00:23.820 --> 00:00:26.140
ecosystems on the planet.

00:00:26.140 --> 00:00:27.720
A place that's
home to everything

00:00:27.720 --> 00:00:30.415
from the most dynamic and
forward-thinking companies

00:00:30.415 --> 00:00:32.040
to the startups
nipping at their heels.

00:00:34.627 --> 00:00:36.850
But we and other
innovators in the area

00:00:36.850 --> 00:00:40.320
got to thinking: what
if we could go further?

00:00:40.320 --> 00:00:42.180
What if we could cut
the time it takes

00:00:42.180 --> 00:00:44.310
for world-changing ideas
is to go from lab bench

00:00:44.310 --> 00:00:45.820
to marketplace?

00:00:45.820 --> 00:00:48.740
Help entrepreneurs find support
to take on the most difficult

00:00:48.740 --> 00:00:50.182
challenges?

00:00:50.182 --> 00:00:52.610
Accelerate growth in the
toughest technologies

00:00:52.610 --> 00:00:56.634
to tackle the toughest problems?

00:00:56.634 --> 00:01:01.130
What could we build to
make this a reality?

00:01:01.130 --> 00:01:04.050
We'd build an accelerator to
help ambitious startups get

00:01:04.050 --> 00:01:09.520
from concept to company and
from prototype to production.

00:01:09.520 --> 00:01:12.420
We'd provide financial support
for innovations that require

00:01:12.420 --> 00:01:15.130
long lead times to develop.

00:01:15.130 --> 00:01:18.010
And we'd establish a network
linking the ecosystems

00:01:18.010 --> 00:01:21.750
of Cambridge, Boston, and
beyond to share vital equipment,

00:01:21.750 --> 00:01:24.750
makerspace and diverse talent.

00:01:24.750 --> 00:01:27.430
We'd rally our colleagues
across the region,

00:01:27.430 --> 00:01:30.850
and together, make more
than financial commitments.

00:01:30.850 --> 00:01:34.125
We would make a pledge to
use our energies, our brains,

00:01:34.125 --> 00:01:39.060
and our skills to push the
boundaries of the possible.

00:01:39.060 --> 00:01:41.740
We would build a new
kind of accelerator.

00:01:41.740 --> 00:01:44.760
One as tough as the
technologies it will drive.

00:01:44.760 --> 00:01:48.560
As revolutionary as the
ideas it will support.

00:01:48.560 --> 00:01:52.760
To do all this, we
would build an Engine.

00:01:52.760 --> 00:01:55.510
[MUSIC PLAYING]

